<title>USA: U.S. House panel sets FY98 US timber sales target.</title>
<headline>U.S. House panel sets FY98 US timber sales target.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. House interior appropriations subcommittee on Tuesday approved a spending bill that called for federal timber sales of 3.8 billion board feet for the 1998 fiscal year.</p>
<p>The U.S. Forest Service's timber sales would be down from more than four billion board feet this year. The overall timber sales have been steadily reduced by Congress from about 12 billion board feet 10 years ago, subcommittee Chairman Ralph Regula, an Ohio Republican, told reporters.</p>
<p>The $13 billion interior spending bill included $1.3 billion for the national forest system, which was a $57 million increase from the 1997 forest budget.</p>
</text>
